kline","invalidate":"a close back above the ~$48.35 head","target":"~$44.65","explanation":"The left shoulder formed around $47.78 on May 26, the head peaked at $48.35 on June 2, and the price is currently forming the right shoulder, having pulled back to ~$47.01. The neckline is roughly at $46.50.","signal":"A confirmed Head and Shoulders pattern could signal a bearish reversal, indicating a potential move lower from the current uptrend.","builtAt":"2026-06-07T16:46:35.135Z"}},"fundamentals":{"name":"UBS Group AG","longBusinessSummary":"UBS Group AG operates as a wealth manager and bank worldwide. It operates through five segments: Global Wealth Management, Personal & Corporate Banking, Asset Management, Investment Bank, and Non-Core and Legacy. The Global Wealth Management segment offers financial services, advice, and solutions; investment management, estate planning, and corporate advice services; and wealth management and banking products and services to private wealth and institutional customers. Its Personal & Corporate Banking segment provides banking, retirement, financing, investments, and strategic transactions to private, corporate, and institutional customers through its branch network and digital channels in Switzerland. The Asset Management segment offers diversified asset management services. Its Investment Bank segment provides equities, foreign exchange, precious metals, research, advisory, and capital markets services to institutional, corporate, financial sponsor, and Global Wealth Management customers, as well as focused rates and credit platform. The company also offers lending products, such as securities-based lending, mortgages, structured products, and tailored solutions; collateralized lending residential and commercial real estate, primarily against securities, residential and commercial real estate, other real assets (such as ships and aircraft), private market and hedge fund interest; and unsecured lending. The company was formerly known as UBS AG and changed its name to UBS Group AG in December 2014. UBS Group AG was founded in 1862 and is headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland.","industry":"Banks - Diversified","sector":"Financial Services","marketCap":154089603072,"trailingPE":16.849463,"forwardPE":11.526635,"pegRatio":0.56,"priceToBook":1.5815501,"priceToSales":3.003052,"profitMargin":17.764,"operatingMargin":31.471002,"grossMargin":0,"returnOnEquity":10.16,"returnOnAssets":0.567,"revenueGrowthYoy":13.8,"earningsGrowthYoy":84.39999999999999,"earningsQuarterlyGrowthYoy":79.7,"debtToEquity":null,"currentRatio":null,"quickRatio":null,"freeCashFlow":null,"operatingCashFlow":null,"totalCash":528411983872,"totalDebt":574302978048,"revenue":51311001600,"dividendYield":2.34,"payoutRatio":32.259998,"beta":0.836,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":49.36,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":30.36,"targetMeanPrice":49.26667,"targetHighPrice":61.8,"targetLowPrice":42,"recommendationKey":"buy","numberOfAnalystOpinions":3,"analystRevisions":{"windowDays":90,"upgrades":1,"downgrades":0,"net":1,"latest":{"firm":"Barclays","action":"up","fromGrade":"Underweight","toGrade":"Equal-Weight","date":"2026-04-20"}},"lastQuarter":{"date":"2026-03-31","period":"-1q","epsActual":0.9506,"epsEstimate":0.82743,"surprisePct":14.89},"earningsHistory":[{"date":"2025-06-30","period":"-4q","epsActual":0.8226,"epsEstimate":0.92276,"surprisePct":-10.850000399999999},{"date":"2025-09-30","period":"-3q","epsActual":0.9179,"epsEstimate":0.60424,"surprisePct":51.910000000000004},{"date":"2025-12-31","period":"-2q","epsActual":0.6702,"epsEstimate":0.67459,"surprisePct":-0.64999997},{"date":"2026-03-31","period":"-1q","epsActual":0.9506,"epsEstimate":0.82743,"surprisePct":14.89}],"revenueHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","value":11983000000},{"date":"2025-06-30","value":11499000000},{"date":"2025-09-30","value":11938000000},{"date":"2025-12-31","value":12199000000},{"date":"2026-03-31","value":13771000000}],"grossProfitHistory":[],"netIncomeHistory":[{"date":"2025-03-31","valu